## Why This Is Asked
Tests mastery of dynamic sequences and range-order statistics with realistic constraints (duplicates, frequent updates). It also probes choice of data structures and practical trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- Implicit treap/rope for dynamic sequence
- Range order statistics with per-subtree frequency structure
- Split/merge semantics to isolate and query subranges
- Duplicate handling and memory considerations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Sketch of rangeKthSmallest using splits
function rangeKth(root, l, r, k) {
  let [a, t] = split(root, l-1);
  let [b, c] = split(t, r-l+1);
  let ans = kthInSubtree(b, k);
  root = merge(a, merge(b, c));
  return {root, ans};
}
```

